SunOS: the socket API (socket, getaddrinfo, gai_strerror) is in libsocket and
libnsl on illumos (Solaris 11.4 has them in libc, the libraries are filters
there), so linking ioquake3 and ioq3ded fails on gai_strerror. The old
Makefile build linked -lsocket -lnsl for sunos; the CMake build lost it.

Upstream: not submitted yet; no issue or pull request about it at
https://github.com/ioquake/ioq3 (checked 2026-11-10).

--- ioq3-87a99d18206e878a20289f05ac3c16005dcae5c3/cmake/platforms/unix.cmake.orig
+++ ioq3-87a99d18206e878a20289f05ac3c16005dcae5c3/cmake/platforms/unix.cmake
@@ -20,3 +20,8 @@
     ${CMAKE_DL_LIBS}    # Dynamic loader
     m                   # Math library
 )
+
+if(CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME STREQUAL "SunOS")
+    # getaddrinfo, gai_strerror, socket: libsocket and libnsl on illumos
+    list(APPEND COMMON_LIBRARIES socket nsl)
+endif()
